{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI CAUGHT A REAL DEFECT THAT EVERY LOCAL RUN MISSED — the test edits were never committed.\n\nGerrit 1230 took a Verified -1. It was NOT a flake, NOT a CANCELLED run, and NOT a coverage-gap\ninfra -1: the default suite failed identically on ubuntu-py3.11/3.12/3.13 and macos-py3.13, four\nplatforms, same step, 3 failed / 8858 passed.\n\nTHE TELL was in the failing test NAME:\n  FAILED tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py::test_start_rung_location_for_a_foreign_family_is_unchanged\nThat name had been RENAMED to ..._is_explicit. CI was therefore running a version of the file that did\nnot contain the rename. The three failures were the exact pre-fix expectations:\n  assert ['bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0'] == ['claude-haiku-4-5', ...]\n  assert ['some-unknown-model']              == ['claude-haiku-4-5', ...]\n  assert 200000 == 1000000\n\nROOT CAUSE, verified not guessed:\n  git status            ->  M tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py\n  git show HEAD:tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py | grep -c _is_explicit  ->  0\n  grep -c _is_explicit tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py                  ->  1\nThe three assertion fixes were edited into the WORKING TREE after the commit was cherry-picked, and\nnever folded into it. The later cherry-pick of the 77ed commit did not object because it touches a\ndifferent file, so nothing surfaced the dirty tree.\n\nWHY LOCAL GREEN PROVED NOTHING: every local run — the 8908-pass run, the mutation check, and the\n8909-pass stacked run — executed the WORKING TREE, which had the edits. The pushed commits did not.\nLocal and CI were testing different trees. This is precisely the \"a green suite on a different tree\nsays nothing about this one\" failure mode, and the guard against it is mechanical, not attentional:\nASSERT `git status --porcelain` IS EMPTY BEFORE RUNNING THE SUITE YOU INTEND TO CITE, and again\nbefore pushing. A suite run against a dirty tree is not evidence about the commit.\n\nFIX APPLIED: stash the edit, reset to the 48b3 commit, restore, `git commit --amend --no-edit` (4\nfiles now, was 3), re-cherry-pick 77ed on top. Both Change-Ids preserved\n(48b3 Ied2d4002c8e60c2e3085203fa63664ea97639ea8, 77ed Ia9e31b9eac4894871b64504f23c618a21b339976), so\nthe re-push updates changes 1229/1230 rather than orphaning them. Working tree verified clean, and the\nre-verification run records the tree-dirty line count alongside the gate exit codes so the evidence\ncannot be separated from the tree it was measured on."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785706816502413001,"uuid":"ead3203f-e398-48fa-9519-c4c538f57a02"}